# Privacy Architecture
File: openOODA/spec/security.oot

This page is the normative privacy law for layers L0 through L7.
Rule 1.5 in rules.oot points here. Section 6 adds four hardware
and desktop boundaries beside the gates in sections 1 through 3.

## 1. CapReg64 sensor and sink split (L0)

The register is one 64-bit word. Layout, from std/sec/capreg.oo and
oodar/sec/cap/caps.h:

- [63:48] epoch16. A stale epoch fails oo_cap_reg64_check.
- [47:40] rights8. Eight rights. Values are listed in section 1.2.
- [39:32] badge8. Scope badge. 0 is the root badge.
- [31:0] caps32. One bit per explicit capability. Bits below are the
  privacy split. oo_cap_bit_index is the authority for the numbers.

Sensor bits capture a sample. They do not export it.

- AudioCap is bit 20. PCM capture and playback.
- CameraCap is bit 21. Camera frames.
- HidCap is bit 23. HID reports and key state.
- WindowCap is bit 24. Wayland surfaces.
- FrameCap is bit 25. DMA-BUF and shared-memory frames.

Sink bits move data out of the capturing process.

- NetCap is bit 0. Network export.
- MetricsCap is bit 11. Process counters and telemetry statistics.
- EnvCap is bit 28. Process environment. The allowed namespace is OODA_*.

A page that holds one sensor bit and one sink bit must call
oo_cap_reg64_check before the sample moves. A failed check returns
nothing. Attenuation (oo_cap_reg64_attenuate) may only drop rights
and capability bits. A child cannot gain a sensor or a sink the
parent does not hold.

## 1.2 rights8 privacy bits

rights8 sits at [47:40]. The mask is 8 bits (0..255).

- 0x01 READ
- 0x02 WRITE
- 0x04 EXEC
- 0x08 DELEGATE
- 0x10 ATTENUATE
- 0x20 REVOKE
- 0x40 (decimal 64) RIGHT_PRIVACY_REDACT
- 0x80 (decimal 128) RIGHT_ZERO_TELEMETRY

The C macros at those two values are OODAR_REG64_RIGHT_SEAL (0x40)
and OODAR_REG64_RIGHT_IMMUTABLE (0x80). This privacy law reads the
same bits as follows.

RIGHT_PRIVACY_REDACT (64): a sensor sample may cross a process
boundary only after redaction. A remote capture of a blackout
surface is a redacted capture (section 2).

RIGHT_ZERO_TELEMETRY (128): the register forbids telemetry export
for its whole life. A metrics or network sink must not carry a
sensor sample, a key, or an analytics endpoint.

oo_cap_reg64_check requires every requested rights bit to be set.
A caller that omits bit 64 or bit 128 does not receive that right.

## 2. oocomp surface redaction and seat guard (L4)

Source: openOODA-DE/oocomp/scanout/net_stream_priv.oo.
Seat model: openOODA-DE/oocomp/wl/obj/seat.oo.

PRIVACY_BLACKOUT is surface flag bit 16.
oocomp_privacy_redact_surface(flags, remote) returns:

- -1 when flags < 0.
- 0 when remote is true and (flags & 16) != 0. The frame is redacted
  and is not placed on a remote stream or a screen share.
- 1 otherwise. Local scanout stays visible. A blackout surface on
  the local display is not blanked by this function.

oocomp_seat_privacy_gate(focused, caller, capture) returns:

- -22 when either surface id is not positive.
- -13 when caller != focused. An unfocused surface must not read
  wl_seat input or the clipboard.
- 2 when capture is active and the caller is the focused surface.
  Return 2 arms the privacy LED.
- 1 when the caller is focused and capture is inactive.

wl_seat_set_focus writes pointer focus only when seat bit 0 is set,
and keyboard focus only when seat bit 1 is set. A negative target
fails closed and leaves the previous focus in place.

oocomp_net_stream_gated admits a stream only when all of these hold:

- The register passes oo_cap_reg64_check for NetCap, FrameCap, and
  WindowCap together.
- Tile size is positive and the rate is in 60..240.
- The seat gate returns a non-negative code.
- Surface redaction returns a non-negative code.

A refused stream has admitted=false and a zero seal. The remote
vis_mode is 0 when the surface carries PRIVACY_BLACKOUT.

## 3. oohat Blue Hat and Black Hat (L7)

Blue Hat is badge 13. oohat_blue_audit_page is the sensor and
exfiltration guard. The page increments wrong_caps when all three
are true:

- The source contains &CameraCap or &AudioCap.
- The source contains &NetCap.
- The source does not contain oo_cap_reg64_check.

wrong_caps must be 0 or the Blue quorum bit stays 0. A kernel path
that holds &NetCap or &ProcessCap is a separate wrong-cap finding.

Black Hat is badge 15. oohat_black_data_vectors is the
zero-telemetry and PII-leak check. The secret count increments when
the source contains any of these needles:

- PRIVATE_KEY, api_key, secret_key, or the text "password =".
- google-analytics, sentry.io, mixpanel.com, or telemetry_upload.

A non-zero secret count is a refusal (exit 2). The cycle does not
reach quorum_mask=255 while that count is positive.

## 4. Duties of L0 through L7

Each layer keeps the sensor bits off the sink bits unless section 1
admits the pair.

- L0 (@openOODA-core): mint CapReg64. oo_cap_bit_index and
  oo_cap_reg64_check are the only bit authority.
- L1 (@openOODA-kernel): do not place NetCap or ProcessCap on a
  kernel page. A driver takes one sensor bit, not a sink. DRAM,
  the memory controller, and USB enumeration follow section 6.
- L2 (@openOODA-OS): a daemon that holds AudioCap does not open
  NetCap on the same page without oo_cap_reg64_check.
- L3 (@openOODA-tools): EnvCap reads stay inside the OODA_* names.
  Do not copy the environment into a network payload.
- L4 (@openOODA-DE): run the blackout redaction and the wl_seat
  focus guard in section 2 before any remote frame leaves. The
  blackout clipboard lease follows section 6.4.
- L5 (@openOODA-apps): accept only an attenuated child register.
- L6 (@openOODA-cloud): carry frames that section 2 already redacted.
  Do not reattach a PRIVACY_BLACKOUT surface on the mesh.
- L7 (@openOODA-agents): Blue Hat and Black Hat in section 3 veto
  the cycle when a guard fails.

## 5. Fail closed

A missing register check, a remote blackout surface, an unfocused
seat read, a telemetry needle, a key needle, a missing DRAM lock
bit, a memory-controller write, a locked-screen USB hotplug, or a
spent blackout paste stops the operation. The refused path exports
nothing. No ambient sensor is valid. No partial frame is a success.

## 6. Hardware and desktop privacy boundaries

Four gates call oo_cap_reg64_check before they admit work. A
failed check returns a zero seal. locked or admitted is false.

### 6.1 Boot DRAM lock (L1 ooboot)

Source: openOODA-kernel/ooboot/bootenv/dram_lock.oo.
boot_dram_lock_req_caps requires MmioCap, PciCap, and TpmCap.
The lock mask is 15: bit 1 BIT_TOM_LOCK (top of memory), bit 2
BIT_REMAP_LOCK (DRAM hole remap), bit 4 BIT_INTERLEAVE_LOCK
(channel and rank interleave XOR), bit 8 BIT_SMRAM_DLCK (SMRAM
D_LCK).
boot_dram_lock_verify_mask is true only when (lock_bits & 15) == 15.
boot_dram_lock_seal_gated refuses on two paths. A failed register
check, tom_mb < 16, remap_base_mb < 0, or interleave_xor <= 0
returns an all-zero state. locked is false and seal is 0. A mask
other than 15 keeps tom_mb and the caller lock_bits. It sets
interleave_hash to 0, locked to false, and seal to 0. A full mask
sets lock_mask to 15 and locked to true. The interleave hash is
oo_pqc_sha3_round(tom_mb * 131 + remap_base_mb,
interleave_xor ^ 15). The seal is oo_pqc_sha3_round(reg64 ^ ih,
(tom_mb << 4) ^ lock_bits ^ epoch).

### 6.2 Post-boot MCT guard (L1 ookernel)

Source: openOODA-kernel/ookernel/mm/dram_mct_guard.oo.
mct_guard_req_caps requires FrameCap, MmioCap, and PciCap.
pci_mct_bdf_write_gate returns -22 when bus is outside 0..255,
dev is outside 0..31, or func is outside 0..7. It returns -13 on
a write when bus is 0 and dev is 0, 24, or 25. Any func in range
matches. Those devices are the host bridge, the data fabric, and
the memory controller. A read returns 0. A write to any other
BDF in range returns 0.
iommu_acs_subpage_guard is the 4 KiB bounce check. It returns
-22 when iova_addr < 4096, iova_addr is not a multiple of 4096,
dma_len <= 0, or dma_len is not a multiple of 4096. It returns
-13 when is_p2p is true and (acs_ctrl_bits & 1) == 0. The source
names that tested mask the ACS upstream-redirection bit. A good
bounce returns 1.
tcb_uarch_isolation_barrier compares badge8 at bits [39:32].
Different badges return 7. Equal badges return 0. Mask 7 names
IBPB, VERW, and L1D_FLUSH. The barrier result is 7 or 0.
dram_row_canary_expected returns 0 when the page is below 4096,
the page is not 4 KiB aligned, or boot_nonce <= 0. A valid page
returns oo_pqc_sha3_round(phys_page_addr, boot_nonce ^ 7919).
dram_mct_scrub_gated admits a scrub when the register check
passes, the BDF gate returns 0, the bounce returns a positive
code, and the observed canary equals the expected canary. The
canary nonce is the epoch. The scrub calls the BDF gate with
func 0, the bounce guard with length 4096, acs_ctrl_bits 1, and
is_p2p true, and the barrier with badge bit 32 flipped. A scrub
past the cap check carries uarch_flush_mask 7. A refusal keeps
the partial flags, with admitted false and seal 0. The seal is
oo_pqc_sha3_round(reg64 ^ exp_c ^ fl_m, (bus << 8) ^ dev ^ epoch).

### 6.3 USB class firewall (L1 oodrv-io)

Source: openOODA-kernel/oodrv-io/usb/usb_class_firewall.oo.
usb_firewall_req_caps requires UsbCap and HidCap.
usb_composite_class_guard returns -22 when base_class <= 0 or
iface_class_mask <= 0. screen_locked returns -13 and freezes
hotplug for every class. base_class == 8 with interface mask
bit 4 or bit 8 and seat_approved false returns -13. Bit 4 is
USB class 2 (network). Bit 8 is USB class 3 (HID). The source
comment names a charger with those hidden interfaces. The
refusal keys on base class 8. Any other in-range input returns
1. usb_firewall_admit_gated returns zeros, admitted false, and
seal 0 when the register check fails or dev_id <= 0. A negative
class guard keeps the device fields with admitted false and
seal 0. The admit seal is oo_pqc_sha3_round(reg64 ^ (dev_id <<
4) ^ base_class, (iface_mask << 8) ^ epoch).

### 6.4 Clipboard burn (L4 ooclip)

Source: openOODA-DE/ooclip/core/ttl_burn.oo.
ooclip_ttl_req_caps requires WindowCap and HidCap.
PRIVACY_BLACKOUT remains surface flag bit 16 from section 2.
ooclip_ttl_check returns -22 when any argument is negative. A
blackout source (flag bit 16) returns -13 when paste_count >= 1
or elapsed_sec > 30. elapsed_sec == 30 stays admitted.
paste_count 0 is the one admitted read. That lease records
max_pastes 1 and ttl_sec 30. A source with the flag clear
returns -13 when elapsed_sec > 3600. elapsed_sec == 3600 stays
admitted. That lease records max_pastes 64 and ttl_sec 3600.
The refusal keys on elapsed time. A live lease returns 1.
ooclip_paste_burn_gated returns max_pastes 0, ttl_sec 0, zeroed
true, admitted false, and seal 0 on a failed register check or
payload_hash <= 0. A negative TTL check is the same zeroed
refusal and keeps that source paste limit and TTL. A live lease
has zeroed false, admitted true, and seal
oo_pqc_sha3_round(reg64 ^ payload_hash ^ max_p, (ttl_s << 8) ^
paste_count ^ epoch).
